needed -- and only loaded -- when \code{organism} is not \code{"hsa"}. Genes without a
one-to-one ortholog are dropped, so the converted sets are smaller than the
human ones; how many survived is reported.

The default conversion \code{method}, \code{"gprofiler"}, queries a web service and so
needs network access. On a machine without it, pass
\code{method = "homologene"}, which resolves locally from a bundled mapping at
the cost of some coverage.
}

